{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DLadderAccelerationComposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderAccelerationComposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Units.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderAccelerationComposition.no_new_critical_time","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderAccelerationComposition.no_new_critical_time","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderAccelerationComposition.lean#L70-L79","doc":"**The collapse.**  No finite composition of a single fixed-order Borel–Leroy\ntransform reaches an order outside the ℤ-multiples of the base — in\nparticular, if the target critical time `s'` is incommensurate with the base\norder `s` (`s' ≠ n·s` for every `n`), no `n`-fold iteration reaches it. This\nis why the refuted fixed-order route cannot be repaired by iteration and a\ngenuine Écalle acceleration kernel between distinct critical times is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderAccelerationComposition.borelLeroyWeight_iterate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderAccelerationComposition.borelLeroyWeight_iterate","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderAccelerationComposition.lean#L57-L68","doc":"**Iteration reaches only ℤ-multiples of the base order.**  Composing the\norder-`s` transform `n` times gives exactly the order-`(n • s)` weight\n`(k!)^{n·s} = ((k!)^s)^n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderAccelerationComposition.borelLeroyWeight_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderAccelerationComposition.borelLeroyWeight_add","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderAccelerationComposition.lean#L49-L55","doc":"**Composition adds orders.** Applying the order-`t` Borel–Leroy transform\nafter the order-`s` one multiplies the weights, i.e. gives the *single*\norder-`(s+t)` transform.  (Requires `(k!) ≠ 0` in `R`, automatic in char 0.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DLadderAccelerationComposition.borelLeroyWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DLadderAccelerationComposition.borelLeroyWeight","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DLadderAccelerationComposition.lean#L44-L47","doc":"The Borel–Leroy acceleration weight of order `s` on the `k`-th coefficient:\n`w_s(k) = (k!)^s`.  Integer order `s : ℤ` over a generic field (`zpow`); the\nreal-order weight is `(k! : ℝ) ^ (s : ℝ)` with the identical additive law. ","signatureChunk":0}]}